--TEST--
An uncaught `Core\Db\DbError` reports Novis's own sentence as its message, and the server's text as `serverMessage` among its properties, when the statement bound no value — `rule:core-classes/db-error`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: Core\Db\DbError
// This statement binds no value, so the error keeps the server's text in `serverMessage`.
// Nothing catches the error, so the report on standard error shows both messages.
var $db = Core\Db::connect("main");
$db->query("select * from nowhere", []);
--FILE nvs.toml--
[capabilities.db]
connect = ["main"]

[db.main]
driver = "sqlite"
path = ":memory:"
--EXPECT--
--EXPECT-ERROR--
{"level":"error","msg":"Core\\Db\\Connection::query: `[db.main]` refused the statement: sqlite ERROR: the database cannot run the statement as it is written (code 1).","fields":{"class":"Core\\Db\\DbError","properties":{"kind":8,"sqlState":null,"driverCode":1,"constraint":null,"sql":"select * from nowhere","serverMessage":"no such table: nowhere"}},"nodes":[{"function":"<script>","file":"case.nvs","line":6}]}
